{"tool_name":"ipick","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"ipick","home":"https://github.com/pokynmr/ipick","license":"BSD-2-Clause","summary":"The iPick program is available as a module for the POKY and NMRFAM-SPARKY. It is highly recommended that you use the module instead of the command line tool. The main reasons are the ease of work and the extended capabilities provided in the module.","addition_date":"2021-09-28T19:13:15.030729Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:18:48.830179Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Desktop application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:ipick","credit":[{"email":"mehdi.rahimi@ucdenver.edu","name":"Mehdi Rahimi","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7812-7333","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"yeongjoon.lee@ucdenver.edu","name":"Yeongjoon Lee","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9156-6477","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"jmarkley@wisc.edu","name":"John L. Markley","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"woonghee.lee@ucdenver.edu","name":"Woonghee Lee","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Peak detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3215"},{"term":"Validation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2428"}]}],"name":"iPick","owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1016/j.jmr.2021.106995","metadata":{"abstract":"Peak picking is a critical step in biomolecular NMR spectroscopy. The program, iPick, presented here provides a scripting tool and a graphical user interface (GUI), which allow the user to perform interactive and intuitive peak picking and validation. The click-and-run GUI requires no computer programming skills, while the scripting tool can be used by more advanced users to customize the application. If used with a multi-core CPU, the multiprocessing feature of iPick reduces the processing time significantly by invoking parallel computing. The GUI is a plugin, compatible with the popular NMRFAM-SPARKY software package and its newly released successor, the POKY software. Features implemented in iPick include automated noise level detection and threshold setting, cross-validation against multiple spectra, and a method for quantifying peak reliability. The iPick software is cross-platform, open-source, and freely available from https://github.com/pokynmr/ipick.","authors":[{"name":"Lee W."},{"name":"Lee Y."},{"name":"Markley J.L."},{"name":"Rahimi M."}],"citationCount":8,"date":"2021-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Journal of Magnetic Resonance","title":"iPick: Multiprocessing software for integrated NMR signal detection and validation"},"pmcid":"PMC8767925","pmid":"34004411","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"NMR","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0593"},{"term":"Transcription factors and regulatory sites","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0749"},{"term":"Workflows","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0769"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"iPick","home":"https://bio.tools/ipick","license":"BSD-2-Clause","summary":"The iPick program is available as a module for the POKY and NMRFAM-SPARKY. It is highly recommended that you use the module instead of the command line tool. The main reasons are the ease of work and the extended capabilities provided in the module.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:ipick/app/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":null,"interpreted":true,"license":null,"public":true,"readme":false,"repository":{"anonymous":null,"online":null}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count